WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 4: Making Things.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:11.860
In this unit, your child learns the words for shapes, colours,
and clothes, and how to make things with paper shapes —

3
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.340
like a paper quilt, a picture, or a shape animal.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.080
They talk about what people are wearing
and dress up in pretend party costumes.

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:26.840
They meet the short ‘e’ sound (hen, pen, tent) and
enjoy the old story of the elves and the shoemaker.

6
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:34.340
The gentle idea running through it all is that making
things takes creativity and patience — and it is fun to try,

7
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.100
try again.

8
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.760
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:48.100
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
point to shapes (square, circle, triangle, rectangle).

10
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.360
you will also name and point to colours
(red, blue, green, yellow, silver, gold…).

11
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.300
you will also name some clothes and
costumes (hat, shirt, dress, clown, king…).

12
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.040
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:08.300
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
square, circle, triangle, rectangle, red, blue.

14
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.900
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.460
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:22.620
The reading sequence includes Amal
Makes a Mat and Talk about Making Things.

17
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:23.980
Read actively.

18
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.920
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.720
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.720
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

21
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.120
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: This is a ___.

22
00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:49.200
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.860
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:58.660
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.160
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.840
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.520
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:14.580
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.300
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.800
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
